# AWS CDK Infrastructure

I help you define infrastructure as code with CDK.

## CDK Stack
```typescript
import * as cdk from 'aws-cdk-lib';
import * as ec2 from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-ec2';
import * as ecs from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-ecs';
import * as ecs_patterns from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-ecs-patterns';

export class MyAppStack extends cdk.Stack {
  constructor(scope: cdk.App, id: string, props?: cdk.StackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);

    // VPC
    const vpc = new ec2.Vpc(this, 'VPC', {
      maxAzs: 2,
      natGateways: 1,
    });

    // ECS Cluster
    const cluster = new ecs.Cluster(this, 'Cluster', { vpc });

    // Fargate Service with ALB
    new ecs_patterns.ApplicationLoadBalancedFargateService(this, 'Service', {
      cluster,
      taskImageOptions: {
        image: ecs.ContainerImage.fromRegistry('my-app:latest'),
        containerPort: 3000,
        environment: {
          NODE_ENV: 'production',
        },
      },
      desiredCount: 2,
      publicLoadBalancer: true,
    });
  }
}
```

## Deploy
```bash
npx cdk synth    # Generate CloudFormation
npx cdk diff     # Preview changes
npx cdk deploy   # Deploy stack
npx cdk destroy  # Tear down
```

## Best Practices
- Use constructs for reusable patterns
- Separate stacks by lifecycle
- Use cdk.context.json for environment config
- Enable cdk-nag for security checks

# AWS Secrets Management

I help you manage secrets securely.

## SSM Parameter Store
```typescript
import { SSMClient, GetParameterCommand, PutParameterCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-ssm';

const ssm = new SSMClient({ region: process.env.AWS_REGION });

// Get secret
async function getSecret(name: string): Promise<string> {
  const response = await ssm.send(new GetParameterCommand({
    Name: name,
    WithDecryption: true,
  }));
  return response.Parameter!.Value!;
}

// Store secret
async function putSecret(name: string, value: string) {
  await ssm.send(new PutParameterCommand({
    Name: name,
    Value: value,
    Type: 'SecureString',
    Overwrite: true,
  }));
}
```

## Secrets Manager
```typescript
import { SecretsManagerClient, GetSecretValueCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager';

const sm = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: process.env.AWS_REGION });

async function getSecretJSON(secretId: string) {
  const response = await sm.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({
    SecretId: secretId,
  }));
  return JSON.parse(response.SecretString!);
}

// Usage
const dbCreds = await getSecretJSON('prod/db/credentials');
const connectionString = `postgres://${dbCreds.username}:${dbCreds.password}@...`;
```

## When to Use Which
| Service | Use Case |
|---------|----------|
| Parameter Store | Config values, feature flags, simple secrets |
| Secrets Manager | Database credentials, API keys with rotation |

# AWS IAM Security

